; The menu's fill, matched to the house's (`scripts/house/lighting.gd::AFTER`,
; and `scenes/house/house_world.tscn`) so that pressing Play is not a jump in
; colour temperature. It was `#F5F0E5` at 0.55 -- a desaturated near-neutral
; that is in no part of ART_BIBLE.md section 3's palette -- and is now
; CREAM -> PEACH at 0.35, the same warm fill the rooms use.
;
; The menu's own SUN is deliberately left alone. Its matrix is correct (it reads
; back as elevation 51.3 degrees, azimuth +34.0, above the horizon, unlike the
; house's, which was transposed and pointing up from under the floor), it is an
; outdoor scene with its own framing, and its shadow is cast on one large open
; plane rather than across pastel walls, which is what the section 7 amendment
; of 2026-09-18 was about. Only the colour is shared.
; "Learn with Aliz": a wide sky-blue banner above the four-button row (a
; fifth square would crowd the row on a phone). DUSTY_BLUE (#9AC0D9) from
; ART_BIBLE section 3, cream rim, the same corner radius family as the row.
; Numbers, from the bottom-anchored SafeArea edge: 700 x 96, from -404 to
; -308 (16 px above the row, which ends at -292). At 1334x750 that is
; x 317..1017, y 330..426; at 2340x1080, x 820..1520, y 660..756.
[sub_resource type="StyleBoxFlat" id="StyleBoxFlat_tutor"]
