; Shadows OFF, 2026-09-20, LOOK pass -- and this is the section 7 amendment of
; 2026-09-18 being APPLIED here rather than overturned anywhere.
;
; That amendment removed the house's directional shadows after an owner review
; on a physical iPhone: at this camera pitch the props threw hard diagonal
; shapes that read as an artefact rather than as grounding. The menu was left
; alone at the time on the argument that its shadow falls on "one large open
; plane rather than across pastel walls". Rendered at 1334x750 and 2340x1080
; and looked at, that argument does not survive the picture: the shadow the menu
; actually casts is Aliz's own, a hard grey-green diagonal slab laid across the
; peach rug, HER OWN LEGS and the baby beside her -- the same artefact, on the
; first screen a child ever sees, at the largest on-screen size any character
; reaches in this game.
;
; The measured before/after is in `docs/LOOK_PASS.md`; the cost REMOVED is a
; directional shadow map plus its depth-only geometry pass every frame, which is
; the one real per-frame saving available in either of these two scenes.
;
; The settings below are KEPT, unchanged and inert, exactly as the amendment
; asks of the house: re-enabling is one character.
[node name="DirectionalLight3D" type="DirectionalLight3D" parent="."]
transform = Transform3D(0.8296, -0.4356, 0.3494, 0, 0.6248, 0.7808, -0.5583, -0.6479, 0.5185, 0, 3, 0)
light_color = Color(1, 0.93464, 0.85752, 1)
light_energy = 0.92
shadow_enabled = false
shadow_opacity = 0.45
directional_shadow_max_distance = 18.0

; The storybook garden -- house, path, flowerbeds, trees, fence, clouds, sun --
; is built in code by `scripts/menu/menu_garden.gd` from palette tokens, so the
; scene file holds no prop colours to drift. See that file.
[node name="Garden" type="Node3D" parent="."]
script = ExtResource("11")

; The two characters -- Aliz (PinkGirlBuddy) and Bunny (BabyLittleBuddy) -- are
; added in code by `main.gd` (`_add_buddy_avatar()`, `_add_bunny()`), through
; the production wrappers, so the title screen shows exactly the cast the child
; is about to play with. No procedural stand-in: `test_buddy_avatar.gd`
; section 8 pins that as a product decision.

